<title>GERMANY: Buba's Hesse says ECB head will not be French.</title>
<headline>Buba's Hesse says ECB head will not be French.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Helmut Hesse said on Thursday it was &quot;completely impossible&quot; that the first head of the planned European Central Bank (ECB) could be French.</p>
<p>Hesse made the comment during a speech at a Hannover university.</p>
<p>Most commentators say that the head of the Dutch central bank Wim Duisenberg, due to take over soon as head of the European Monetary Institute, is the natural candidate to be the first president of the ECB.</p>
<p>But there has been recent talk that France might want to see somebody French in the job, in return for the decision to site the bank in Frankfurt.</p>
<p>(( --Bonn Newsroom +49 228 26097150 ))</p>
</text>
